Z||000003||1FST2M6||03-03-2000||10:21 PM||||An ATI P600B would do just fine... you'll have to make a belt tightening brace (idler pulley) but the cooler charge from the intercooler would allow you to run up to 9psi without any major mods.. assuming your not to high on the current compression ratio what are you running?.. there is a Canadian Firm that carrys all the parts for a Centrigufal supercharger install... i'll have to go find said page.. more to follow soon.. for more information on flowrates and ideas you might want to contact the shop i deal with Engineered Performance Inc. <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  I'll go find that other page... and <A HREF="http://www.procharger.com" TARGET=_blank>www.procharger.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||BBBAD GT||03-03-2000||10:48 PM||||I've only found one supercharger kit for the V6, from some outfit in Canada (they still haven't responded to my emails yet).  It looked like a procharger, and they said it was for non-AC cars only.  I own a vortech on my Stang, and even their entry level blower (the A trim) would maybe be too big for the small V6, vortech does make smaller blowers for small displacement motors.  <P>From what I've seen so far, it looks like a Turbo option would be better suited for the V6, because of the placement of the exhaust manifolds into one and all that space on the pass side of the motor.  Please post if you ever do see a blower on the V6, I'd be very interested.<P> <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Brian Olsovsky||03-03-2000||10:52 PM||||no offense, but hearing that turbo crap is getting old. all my friends are rice burners.boooooooo...hissssssssss||||reg||13
Z||000006||BBBAD GT||03-03-2000||11:02 PM||||hehe...no offense taken.....but I was just telling you what I've seen lately, which is not much (if any) blower guys and many many either backyard or custom built turbos for the V6.  Don't get me wrong, I love my blower on my Stang, and I'd never go back to naturally aspirated again.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BTW, if you are interested, I've made a "Basic Blower Tech" page for the Stang at  <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/JeffHTML4.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/JeffHTML4.htm</A>  if you want some background on blower tuning.||||reg||1
