Z||000008||1FST2M6||03-03-2000||11:40 PM||||SWEET setup ya got BBad! I've been talking with the guys at PMS about a retro fit unit for the Fiero (they are at the shop often) PMS is as you know located in Acworth, Ga about 10 minutes from my house and 20 from the shop. The Vortech S/FMU has been brought to my attention too... under nitrous my intake will show .61lb of positive pressure just because of the rapidly expanding  gas.. Not sure why i explained it you know what it does.. I currently have a Stillen Vacuum fuel pressure riser and under nitrous or any operation we can't tell a difference with this unit installed? Still holds about 108-111psi with the nitrous on and about 85-90 with it off... might the vortech unit fix my problem... we're looking for a more gradual pressure increase... not this "...OH MY FRREEKING GOD  thats a lot of black smoke then lots of tire bouncing/squeeling etc.. if we could just hold it back a 1/2 second it would help...  any ideas...  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||BBBAD GT||03-04-2000||12:00 AM||||Thanks for the compliment.  I'm not sure how your N2O is working with your fuel pressure regulator (I assume you have a NOS dry flow kit).  I've only used wet flow kits, which doesn't monkey with the injectors.  Are you running 85-90 psi of fuel pressure normally?  Am I missing something,because this sounds awfully high.  The computer would have a tough time pulling back the pulse rate for that pressure for it to have a relatively "ok" A/F ratio based on the O2 sensors.  I bet you have been hooked up to a wide ban O2 sensor, what are the readings on/off the N2O? The super FMU only references boost, so I'm not sure if it would work with your N2O combo.  Off the subject question...how are you handleing your timing retard with the N2O, if any?      ||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||03-04-2000||12:25 AM||||I am running 85-90 all the time.. and go through O2s like their going out of style! Lucky for me AutoZone says bosch has a life time warranty... I kill the ceramic inside of a sensor in about 1 bottle! and have trashed a cat... with only 2000 miles on it! It is a dry Manifold kit. Thought about foggers but couldn't justify the expense at the time, regret it now...  But the new chip and progressive controller have both, made the car run (#1) and (#2) puts me in the stupid fast don't mess with him catagory on the local gimp civic scene... Guess i just have to break down and buy a PowerDyne or a J-trim.  Anyone want to buy a nitrous kit? Part#05120  Intake jet .052 and bypass of .038... Super Hi-Flo valve with pressure guage and blanket, injector upgrade required...  $400    <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-04-2000).]||||reg||1
